# A recipe's render (tools/make_manual.py --renders): from P1, headphones, Pitch lock off, Scene time 0. The two high
# sines are set up before the recording (the moves take ~8 s); the clip starts on them, then strikes them.
# "# @" marks the listening times (tools/make_manual.py --times).
notips
phones 1
set 74 0
set 71 0
tapkey w0
tap PLAY
wait 2500
tap EDIT
turn K1 -40 60
turn K3 -40 60
tap HOME
tap HOME
turn K1 35 60
turn K3 36 60
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap HOME
turn K2 30 60
turn K4 30 60
wait 1500
tapkey b10
tapkey b10
tap LFO
tap LFO
turn K4 30 80
wait 1000
wav bells.wav
# @ Two pure sines, high, a tritone apart, bending each other at X-mod 70: one metallic tone that never stops ringing
wait 1500
# @ The cutoffs down to about 300 Hz, LFO I on Roundtooth at 0.4 Hz on both cutoffs, the sends to -100: struck
tap HOME
turn K2 -24 25
turn K4 -25 25
tap LFO
tap LFO
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
turn SELECT 29 40
tapkey b7
tapkey b7
shot bells-0.png
turn K2 -50 10
turn K4 -15 20
# @ A bell struck every 2.5 s: bright on the hit, the top dying first
wait 14000
shot bells-1.png
wavstop
